What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/modulator_frequency
KernelVersion:	7.4
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Sets the requested device-wide ADC modulator frequency in Hz. The
		selected frequency and corresponding power mode are applied when
		buffered capture starts. The available frequencies are derived from
		the input master clock and the MCLK divider settings supported by the
		device.

		The output sampling frequency of each channel is the modulator
		frequency divided by that channel mode's digital filter decimation
		ratio. Changing the modulator frequency preserves each channel's
		decimation setting and updates its requested sampling frequency. It
		also changes the set of available per-channel sampling frequencies.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/modulator_frequency_available
KernelVersion:	7.4
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Reading returns the list of device-wide ADC modulator frequencies
		available with the current input master clock, in Hz.
